{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3MLDWHcziUbmX4xdctS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ticket 01 is done. With a freshly rebuilt `dist/`, `build:hydration`, `test:hydration` (17 tests), `test:hydration-dev` (17) and `test:e2e` (12) all pass. `test:build` (39), `test:ssr`, `test:plugins`, lint and the full `npm test` (286) also pass.\n\nThere were two parts to the fix:\n\n1. **The build itself.** `example-hydration/vite.config.ts` loads the plugin from `../dist/vite.js` again instead of `../src/vite.js`. The README and AGENTS.md already said `dist`, so the README is unchanged and `toc:hydration` didn't need running.\n2. **The misleading error.** `src/build.ts` now shows the \"install typescript\" message only when Node fails to find the module by its plain name, `'typescript'`. Any other failure to load it now says `require` is unavailable or unusable and to load the entry from its built form. The original error is kept as the cause.\n\nThe real failure isn't quite what the ticket describes. Inside a Vite config bundle, `require` does exist, but Vite hands it a `file://` path to TypeScript. Node can't load that and reports \"module not found\", which is the same error code as a genuinely missing package. So an \"is `require` undefined\" check wouldn't have caught it. That check also can't work after bundling, because esbuild always defines its own `require` stand-in.\n\nI added three tests in `test/build.ts` that run real processes:\n- **No `require`:** the entry, run as ESM, gets the built-form message.\n- **TypeScript really missing:** run from an empty temp directory, it still gets the \"install typescript\" message.\n- **Vite config:** a small config in `test/fixtures/vite-config-src/` imports the plugin from source and gets the built-form message, not the TypeScript one.\n\nThe tests call esbuild through its command line because its JS API breaks when bundled into the test. I also corrected AGENTS.md's explanation of why the config must import from `dist`. My notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, uncommitted.\n\nThere are three commits on the branch, nothing pushed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":73760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc64cd6a-3638-45e4-b70b-6a40470d9ff5","uuid":"d776d0ad-a346-457d-8a17-c557ecd64c19","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:57:48.666Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3MLDDfw9rASsJHLt8jt"}
